# AI OCR Receipt Extraction Engine — Architecture & Implementation Plan

An enterprise-grade, high-throughput AI OCR pipeline designed for the **Yatra Expense Module**. It enables concurrent extraction of up to **5 receipts or bills**, persists raw extracted data into JSON format, applies strict business-logic filtering to distill required expense fields, and renders a batch review interface in the UI — all engineered to execute within a strict **2–3 second SLA** with **zero fallbacks**.

---

## 1. Executive Summary & Design Constraints

| Constraint / Requirement | Engineering Solution |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Throughput & Capacity** | Batch upload of up to **5 receipts/bills** in a single user action. |
| **Strict Latency SLA (2–3 sec)** | **Concurrent asynchronous pipeline** (`asyncio.gather` + worker concurrency) with in-memory image optimization. Images are processed in parallel, not sequentially. |
| **Two-Phase Extraction & Filtering** | **Stage 1**: Full multimodal OCR extraction to raw structured JSON (`raw_text`, line items, taxes, merchant, timestamps) persisted to disk/DB.<br>**Stage 2**: Filtering engine extracts only required fields (`vendor`, `amount`, `gst`, `category`, `date`, `time`, `payment_mode`, `description`). |
| **Zero Fallback Policy** | Absolutely **no mock/synthetic fallbacks**, no hardcoded dummy vendors, no fake toll/fuel defaults. Every error (corrupt image, unreadable receipt, network/API failure) produces a structured validation failure with explicit error feedback. |
| **User Experience (UI)** | Multi-receipt batch upload dropzone, live latency timer, card-based side-by-side review of filtered fields, batch "Confirm & Add All" to agency expenses. |

