## 6. Zero Fallbacks Policy & Strict Error Handling

> [!IMPORTANT]
> In accordance with the system rule of **zero fallbacks in any step**, the pipeline operates on deterministic validation:
> 1. **No Mock Data**: The legacy mock implementation in `backend/routers/agency_expenses.py:extract_ocr_receipt` that returned fake "Shell Fuel Station" or "Himalayan Lodge" data will be completely eliminated.
> 2. **Authentication / Key Validation**: If the AI model service key is invalid or unavailable, the endpoint returns an explicit `503 Service Unavailable` with descriptive error details, rather than quietly faking an extraction.
> 3. **Format & Integrity Validation**: Corrupt or unparsable images fail with explicit `422 Unprocessable Entity` stating the specific file that could not be decoded.
> 4. **Item-Level Failures in Batch**: If 4 out of 5 receipts succeed and 1 is completely unreadable (e.g. blank black image), the response returns 4 valid filtered records and 1 structured failure entry with `status: "failed", error: "No legible text or receipt detected"`. It never fabricates fallback numbers.

